PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key facts unchanged: cholesterol obligatory for ecdysone (trace amounts), cholestanol supplies only bulk/structural role (adult survival = 0 alone), 2 mg/L cholesterol insufficient alone, maternal sterol deposits finite and diet-dependent. 

Round 2: 9/10 colleagues converge on H (Col1-9), with Col7 switching from C. Core argument: maternal cholesterol reserve supports larval molts + pupation on pure 250 mg/L cholestanol but exhausted before adult eclosion; zero maternal reserve + 2 mg/L cholesterol yields outright larval death. Only Col10 retains C, arguing maternal reserve insufficient even for pupation (larval death) and Q2 fails at eclosion. 

Disagreements now minimal: solely on depletion timing (pre-pupation death vs. post-pupation/no-eclosion). H best fits concentration thresholds, zero adult survival clause, and maternal-reserve logic; C underestimates maternal load. No contradictions with problem wording. Current lean strengthened: H. Unresolved: exact larval/pupal stage at which reserve is exhausted.}

